# .gitignore — FieldSnap NZ
#
# Rule of thumb: commit project source, dependency lockfile, tests and the lean
# technical docs; ignore generated output, local tool state, credentials and
# third-party reference material.

# --- Dart / Flutter generated ---
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
build/
*.iml
.flutter-devtools/

# --- Android / Gradle generated ---
android/.gradle/
android/.kotlin/
android/local.properties
android/app/debug/
android/app/profile/
android/app/release/
android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
captures/
.gradle/

# --- Python caches (tools/ scripts) ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- IDE / OS ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets / local config ---
*.env
.env.*
*.pem

# --- Course material and reference-only inputs ---
# Milestone 1 PDF, lecture slides, other students' examples and any participant
# data live here locally and must not be published to GitHub.
reference/

# --- Usability session data (participant privacy) ---
# Per-participant sheets, transcripts and any recording stay local. Only aggregate results are
# published, in docs/usability_evaluation_report.md.
docs/usability/results/
*.m4a
*.wav
*.docx
*.pptx

# --- Photography data set (1A) ---
# Downloaded images stay local: their licences allow use but the repository should
# not become a redistribution mirror, and re-downloading is reproducible from the
# manifest plus tools/fetch_dataset.py. Only the scripts and the protocol are
# versioned; data/split_protocol.json and data/class_indices.json are small enough
# to commit deliberately (see below).
data/raw/
data/cache/
data/manifest.csv
data/manifest_train.csv
data/manifest_val.csv
data/manifest_test.csv
data/split.json

# --- Vendored plugin's own test fixtures (upstream test assets, not our model) ---
third_party/tflite_flutter/example/
third_party/tflite_flutter/test/

# --- Exported model binaries and fixtures ---
# The INT8 model that actually ships is committed (1.2 MiB) so the app and the tests can be
# run without retraining; the float model and the Keras checkpoint are not needed for that
# and are regenerated by tools/train_and_export.py.
artifacts/qg/
artifacts/conf/
artifacts/memory/
artifacts/*.tflite
artifacts/*.keras

# --- Large or unlicensed binaries ---
*.lite
*.zip
# Model binaries are excluded individually above rather than by extension, so the one
# model that ships (assets/models/fieldsnap_int8.tflite) can be committed on purpose.
